  "method": {
    "timing": "Fresh session open through receipt of Wasm, warm files, eight frontend workers in every run. Matched live/pinned/two-physical-CPU cases rotated and reversed through six orderings, six rounds with and six without --profile. taskset -c 0,1 limits the entire test process tree. Session build timeout 12 seconds.",
    "scheduling": "Read Linux /proc/thread-self/schedstat on worker exit; sum runnable wait and on-CPU time over all 14 exiting children (seven parse, seven checking). Excludes parent lane. CPU column is wait4 user+system for the Deno driver and all reaped descendants. Host pressure is the fraction of the trial during which any runnable task was stalled for CPU, from /proc/pressure/cpu. CPU and child wait columns sum concurrent work and cannot be added to elapsed time.",
    "oneCpu": "Separate four paired profiled builds on the subsequently edited live checkout (a5e6d133); each pair used the same output. taskset -c 0 controlled the available CPU count. Reported separately from f9fae42d.",
    "natural": "Eight more runs without an affinity limit, on the immutable snapshot, as competing workloads ran. OS scheduling was observed rather than controlled in these eight runs.",
    "graph": "Read the native checked queue after all jobs completed. Validated all 276 module IDs and all 2390 dependency edges against a depth-first walk in loader source order, including reexports, asset modules and implicit prelude edges. Decoded worker packet tail with project_packet_codecs field order and verified counter sums against the compiler. Check, publish and lower CPU sums match the official worker CPU total for every profiled run.",
    "criticalPath": "Model is the longest path in the observed DAG, weighted by the median of per-run check plus interface-publication CPU for each module. It excludes setup, serial assembly, lowering after publication and OS delays. Scenarios that shorten a weight hold all other costs and edges fixed. Six additional traces recorded actual claim, first interface ready and job finish using timestamps at the native queue mutex release. Every observed consumer started after every required interface was ready.",
    "fill": "Timed unmodified, out-of-line libc memset(value=0, size>=1024) returning into capability_contracts.instantiate/instantiateBody in the release binary. Sum of wall intervals across calls on all workers, including clock overhead and descheduling. Separate six profiled-process-independent runs on archived f9fae42d. Inline stores and nonzero fills are excluded."
  },
